GCC Regulatory Mapping: NCA ECC, SAMA, NESA, ISR
Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Design and implement a normalized relational schema for multi-framework regulatory control mapping
Import and reconcile heterogeneous GCC regulator control catalogs (NCA ECC, SAMA CSF, NESA/SIA, Qatar NIA)
Build a crosswalk engine linking GCC controls to NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5 and ISO 27001:2022
Engineer logic to flag GCC-specific overlay requirements (data residency, Arabic-language logging, local hosting)
Generate a queryable regional applicability matrix supporting CGRC Domain 6 (Continuous Monitoring) reporting
Prerequisites
Strong SQL skills (joins, CTEs, window functions)
Working knowledge of NIST SP 800-53 and ISO 27001 control structures
Familiarity with GRC concepts: control inheritance, overlays, compensating controls
Python 3.10+ scripting experience (pandas, sqlite3/psycopg2)
Understanding of CGRC Domain 6 (Compliance Monitoring and Reporting)
Comfort working with CSV data of unknown/inconsistent schemas
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine via Start Lab. Provision the environment:

sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y postgresql postgresql-contrib python3-pip sqlite3
pip3 install pandas psycopg2-binary sqlalchemy openpyxl
sudo systemctl enable --now postgresql
sudo -u postgres createdb gcc_grc_map
mkdir -p ~/gcc-lab/{data,scripts,output} && cd ~/gcc-lab
You will source or construct representative control catalog CSVs for each framework (NCA ECC 2-2024, SAMA CSF v2.0, NESA/SIA, Qatar NIA v2.0) — sample small extracts (10-15 controls each) are acceptable given no single public unified dataset exists. Structure them consistently: control_id, domain, title, description, control_type.

Tasks
Task 1: Design and Populate the Normalized Control Database
Architect a schema that avoids duplication and supports many-to-many crosswalks across frameworks.

Required entities (minimum):

frameworks (id, name, version, jurisdiction, authority)
controls (id, framework_id, control_ref, domain, title, description)
crosswalks (source_control_id, target_control_id, mapping_strength: enum[exact,partial,related], rationale)
overlays (id, name, description, trigger_condition)
control_overlays (control_id, overlay_id)
Design decisions you must make and justify in comments:

How do you model many-to-many crosswalks bidirectionally without duplicate rows?
How do you version controls if a framework updates (e.g., NCA ECC 1-2018 to 2-2024)?
How do you handle controls with no equivalent in another framework (orphan handling)?
